    "notes": "A flow-controlled shot on a steeply declining temperature: 86.5 °C for a two-second temperature-compensation fill, 81.5 °C through puck wetting, then 61.5 °C for the pour.\n\nFrames 1 and 2 run at 4 ml/s and hand over as soon as pressure passes 5 bar, so the preinfusion length follows the puck rather than a fixed time. The pour then opens up to 7 ml/s but is held to a 2 bar ceiling, so flow is limited by resistance rather than by the pump. Default target is 45 g.\n\nThe declining temperature is the point of the profile — the puck sees progressively cooler water as extraction proceeds. Dial with grind first; the pressure ceiling means a too-fine puck shows up as a slow pour rather than a pressure spike.\n\n(Bundled from the reaprime default set, author Decent. It shipped without notes; the description above is read from the profile's own frames. What PSPH stands for is not recorded in de1app, reaprime or Visualizer.)",
